    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0316" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/146</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schmedeman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 203</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Christiania</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 25</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that, at a meeting of the Storthing on April 14 last, a petition of the Ford
                    Peace Conference to the effect that the governments of neutral nations should be
                    called upon to take the initiative for the calling of an official conference of
                    these nations for the purpose of bringing about peace, was presented by one of
                    the members of the Storthing. The reading of the petition was granted, but, as
                    there was no quorum, it was postponed until May 2. After the reading, a motion
                    was made by the president of the Storthing, Mr. Mowinckel, that the petition be
                    laid on the table. This motion was carried against 13 votes.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. G. Schmedeman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
